            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0774" n="678" xml:id="pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">423.11 L 23/318: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-09T09:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1921—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:59 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>27. <hi rendition="#italic">In re</hi> Landreau claim. Is there any objection
                    part United States to Commission sitting in country third member or president of
                    board? It is argued this would enable more distinguished man to be secured.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
